# The trust boundary: files that decide what the agents may do, what CI checks, what ships and what is spent.
# Everything else has no code owner, so the Foundry's approved work still merges by itself once green.
# This only takes effect when the ruleset on main turns on "require review from code owners", which waits for the
# agents' own GitHub identity (docs/DELIVERY.md, "Who the agents are"). Until then it requests no reviews: the
# agents open their pull requests as Nikita, and nobody is asked to review their own work.
/.github/                   @nikitapage10
/.claude/                   @nikitapage10
/CLAUDE.md                  @nikitapage10
/vercel.json                @nikitapage10
/package.json               @nikitapage10
/package-lock.json          @nikitapage10
/api/_world/budget.ts       @nikitapage10
/scripts/foundry-watch.sh   @nikitapage10
